class.description:
[SettingsServerManager] keeps one [SettingsServer] per domain, finds them by name and has "all" methods ([method load_all], [method save_all], [method apply_all], [method revert_all], [method reset_all_to_defaults]) for menus such as "Reset all settings". It also starts the servers while the game starts: for each server it captures the defaults, loads the settings file and applies the values, so that the settings of the player are active before the first scene.
[b]Startup phases.[/b] A server is started in the phase returned by [method SettingsServer.get_apply_phase]:
- [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_PHASE_PRE_DISPLAY]: right after the servers and modules are registered, before [DisplayServer] is created. Values that the window needs at creation belong here.
- [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_PHASE_SERVERS]: after the script languages are initialized and the default bus layout is loaded. This is the default.
- [constant SettingsServer.APPLY_PHASE_SCENE]: in the start of the game after the root window is set up, before the main scene is loaded and before the autoloads are ready. The script domains from [member ProjectSettings.settings/startup/custom_servers] are created in this phase.
After each phase, [signal startup_applied] is emitted. A server that is registered after its phase has already passed (for example by a GDExtension) is started at once.
Startup only happens in games, not in the editor and the project manager, and only if [member ProjectSettings.settings/startup/apply_on_startup] is [code]true[/code]. When the game exits, queued autosaves are written and the servers created from [member ProjectSettings.settings/startup/custom_servers] are freed.
[codeblocks]
[gdscript]
func _ready():
	print(SettingsServerManager.get_domains()) # For example ["audio", "game"].

	var game = SettingsServerManager.get_server(&"game")
	if game:
		game.value_changed.connect(func(name, value): print("%s = %s" % [name, value]))

func _on_reset_all_pressed():
	SettingsServerManager.reset_all_to_defaults()

func _on_apply_pressed():
	SettingsServerManager.apply_all()
	if SettingsServerManager.has_dirty_servers():
		print("Some values could not be applied.")
[/gdscript]
[csharp]
public override void _Ready()
{
    GD.Print(string.Join(", ", SettingsServerManager.GetDomains()));

    var game = SettingsServerManager.GetServer("game");
    if (game != null)
    {
        game.ValueChanged += (name, value) => GD.Print($"{name} = {value}");
    }
}

private void OnResetAllPressed()
{
    SettingsServerManager.ResetAllToDefaults();
}

private void OnApplyPressed()
{
    SettingsServerManager.ApplyAll();
    if (SettingsServerManager.HasDirtyServers())
    {
        GD.Print("Some values could not be applied.");
    }
}
[/csharp]
[/codeblocks]
[b]Note:[/b] The API is for the main thread. The registry itself can be read from other threads.
